\begin_layout Standard
The second major problem i set out to tackle is price endogeneity.
 This is generally suspected with OLS estimation since unobserved quality can correlate positively with both market share and price (conditional on regressors) and thus breaking the exogeneity assumption.
 Therefore I introduce instrument variables for prices denoted 
\begin_inset Formula $z_{jt}$
\end_inset

.
 The identifying assumptions are 
\emph on
orthogonality
\emph default
 (i.e.
 
\begin_inset Formula $\mathbb{E}\left[z_{jt}\xi_{jt}\right]=0$
\end_inset

) and 
\emph on
relevance
\emph default
 (i.e.
 
\begin_inset Formula $Cov(p_{jt},z_{jt}\mid\mathbf{x}_{jt})\neq0$
\end_inset

)
\end_layout

